  "name": "ZnT8 (ZINC TRANPORTER8) ANTIBODY",
  "code": "1847",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>High levels of ZnT8 autoantibody (&gt; or =10 AU/mL) is supportive of:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Diagnosis of type 1 diabetes</li>\n<li>High risk for future development of diabetes</li>\n<li>A current or future need for insulin therapy in patients with diabetes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br><strong>Clinical Utility:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>ZnT8A is a marker of childhood-onset type 1diabetes.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Negative results do not exclude the diagnosis of or future risk for type 1 diabetes mellitus.</p>\n<p><br><strong>References:&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Kit Insert</li>\n<li>Bingley PJ: Clinical applications of diabetes antibody testing. J Clin Endocrinol Metab 2010;95:25-33</li>\n</ul>",
